PTX splitk-fence-red-cumulative
"Stream-K fixup: workers store partials to global workspace, named barrier, then the leader does fence.acq_rel.gpu and red.relaxed.gpu.add on the lock; in the peer CTA the leader spins with ld.acquire.gpu, named barrier, then workers read the partials (CUTLASS barrier.h:116-124, 155-162, 185-192; sm90_tile_scheduler_stream_k.hpp:504-546). The fence must release other threads' writes ordered by the barrier. Expected: forbidden."
{
w=0;
l=0;
P2:r0=0;
P3:r1=0;
}
 P0@cta 0,cluster 0,gpu 0 | P1@cta 0,cluster 0,gpu 0 | P2@cta 1,cluster 0,gpu 0 | P3@cta 1,cluster 0,gpu 0 ;
 st.weak.global w, 1      | bar.sync 1, 2            | ld.acquire.gpu r0, l     | bar.sync 1, 2            ;
 bar.sync 1, 2            | fence.acq_rel.gpu        | bar.sync 1, 2            | ld.weak.global r1, w     ;
                          | red.relaxed.gpu.add l, 1 |                          |                          ;
exists
(P2:r0 == 1 /\ P3:r1 == 0)
